  "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\u2202A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
  "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\u2202A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\u2202A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/b1074330fc650cf6af682f173f50943d779819afa59bf5be19edb88def1ef03a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\u2202A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16\\,}.\n$$",
